    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d680">

                <pb facs="0801" n="715" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg715"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCormick to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-10"><hi rendition="#italic">November 10,
                        1903</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 62.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s No. 56,
                    of October 22, 1903, I have the honor to inclose herewith translations from the
                    Russian code pertaining to the recognition by Russian law of Jewish divorces
                    granted by Jewish rabbis, which were made for me by Mr. Berline, an attorney in
                    good standing and by birth himself a Hebrew.</p>
                <p>In addition to the memorandum sent to me by Mr. Berline, the translation of which
                    is inclosed, he writes that the Russian law recognizes all certificates of
                    birth, marriage, divorce, and death issued by Jewish rabbis, as well as all
                    certificates given by ministers of the Jewish faith abroad to Russian Jewish
                    subjects.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert S.
                    McCormick.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d680-a1.xml" xpointer="d680-a1"/>
